I was thinking about the ring of conflict, too.  (Ooh, smell that smoke....) :)
Why should the wearer be immune to attacks from those it enrages?  How about
making it work something like this:

(1) Limit its range to, say, 3 squares.  This was mentioned earlier by someone
    else.

(2) Anything except the wearer which is within range is automatically made
    hostile, and will attack anything bordering on it.

#2 includes such things as the player's pet (if any), which would discourage
wearing the ring while exploring.  Also, the player would at best have a 1 in
8 chance of being attacked by a neighboring monster while wearing it, and
usually higher (depending on how many neighbors the hostile monster has).

